SEG = "CAR"
CAT = "fvicCarriage"
Q = [
    ("Under s 130, is the inside of a car parked on a public street a public place?",
     "Yes, it counts as one", ["No, it is private property", "Only with the windows down", "Only if the engine runs"],
     "Section 130(2) says the interior and exterior of any vehicle, vessel or aircraft in a public place is itself a public place, so a loaded firearm in it is an offence."),
    ("Your rifle's chamber is empty but a loaded detachable magazine is fitted. Under s 130 the rifle is:",
     "Treated as loaded", ["Treated as unloaded", "Loaded only if cocked", "Loaded only if the safety is off"],
     "Section 130(7) defines loaded to include a firearm fitted with a magazine loaded with ammunition that the firearm's own parts can feed into the chamber."),
    ("Outside a public place, s 130 makes it an offence to carry a loaded firearm when you do so:",
     "Recklessly, without regard for safety", ["Without a current club membership", "Before sunrise or after sunset", "In any calibre over .22"],
     "Section 130(1A)(b) makes it an offence to carry a loaded firearm in any other place with reckless disregard for the safety of any person."),
    ("You want to cross a private paddock with your rifle to reach your hunting spot. Under s 131 you need:",
     "The owner or occupier's consent", ["A Game Licence endorsement", "A permit from local police", "A neighbour's signed note"],
     "Section 131(1) makes it an offence to possess, carry or use a firearm on private property without the consent of the owner or occupier."),
    ("Under s 131, which is a defence to carrying a firearm on private property without consent?",
     "Walking a set path to ask", ["Not having fired a single shot", "Keeping the firearm in its case", "Having fired only from a road"],
     "Section 131(2) gives a defence if you were approaching the owner's or occupier's residence along a defined path to ask for consent."),
    ("Firing a shot across a neighbour's property without the owner's or occupier's consent is:",
     "An offence under s 131", ["Lawful if nobody is home", "Lawful from a public road", "Lawful for pest animals"],
     "Section 131(1)(b) makes it an offence to discharge a shot, bullet or other missile onto or across private property without the owner's or occupier's consent."),
    ("A hunter crosses licensed Crown land to reach land that can only be reached that way, to hunt under the Wildlife Act. Section 131(4) says they:",
     "Need no consent to cross", ["Need the lessee's written consent", "Must unload and case the firearm", "Must notify the council first"],
     "Section 131(4) says a licensed person crossing licensed Crown land, to hunt on land that can only be accessed over it, need not obtain consent from the holder of the Crown land licence."),
    ("A medicine your doctor prescribed warns against operating machinery. Under s 132 and the course material, carrying a firearm while affected is:",
     "Against the law", ["Lawful if it is prescribed", "Lawful on private land", "Lawful at half a dose"],
     "Section 132(1) bars carrying or using a firearm under the influence of liquor or a drug, and the course slides say this includes legal and prescription drugs with machinery warnings."),
    ("Your rifle is stolen from your locked garage. You must tell the Chief Commissioner within:",
     "24 hours of learning of it", ["7 days of learning of it", "14 days of learning of it", "28 days of learning of it"],
     "Section 140(1) requires notice of any loss, theft or destruction of a firearm in your possession within 24 hours after you become aware of it."),
    ("You move house and your firearms go with you. Under s 139, you must notify in writing within:",
     "14 days", ["24 hours", "7 days", "28 days"],
     "Section 139 requires written notice within 14 days of a change to your residence, postal address or the address where your firearms are ordinarily stored."),
    ("The Victoria Police course slides say a change of storage address will trigger:",
     "A storage inspection", ["A new safety course", "A fresh 28-day wait", "A licence category review"],
     "The longarm course slides say notice of a change of storage address will trigger a firearm storage inspection."),
    ("A police officer with grounds to suspect you are in possession of a firearm shows ID and asks for your licence. Under s 150 you:",
     "Must produce it", ["May refuse until home", "Need only give your name", "Must first see a warrant"],
     "Section 150 lets a police officer with reasonable grounds who produces identification demand your licence, and you must comply."),
    ("Besides police, the course slides say who can demand your firearm licence in the field?",
     "A Conservation Act authorised officer", ["Any landowner you meet", "A shooting club secretary", "A licensed firearms dealer"],
     "The slides name an authorised officer under s 83 of the Conservation, Forests and Lands Act 1987 as well as police members."),
    ("The Firearm Safety Code booklet says that whenever you carry your firearm you must have with you:",
     "Your current firearms licence", ["Your certificate of registration", "Your permit to acquire", "Your club membership card"],
     "The booklet says you must have your current firearms licence with you whenever you carry your firearm."),
    ("Your mate holds only a category A licence. Under s 127, letting him fire your bolt action .243 on your farm is:",
     "An offence", ["Lawful under your supervision", "Lawful on private land", "Lawful for one shot"],
     "Section 127(1) bars the possessor of a category A or B longarm from letting an unauthorised, non-exempt person carry or use it. Supervised use without a licence is exempt only at an approved range."),
    ("Under Schedule 3, an unlicensed adult may shoot a category A rifle without a licence only when:",
     "Instructed at an approved range", ["Supervised on any farm", "Shooting rabbits on Crown land", "Using a friend's firearm at home"],
     "Schedule 3 item 5 exempts a person of 18 or over receiving instruction from a category A or B licence holder under immediate supervision at an approved shooting range."),
    ("A 14-year-old with no licence wants to try target shooting. Under Schedule 3 this is possible at an approved range under immediate supervision and with:",
     "A parent's written consent", ["A school's written consent", "A current Game Licence", "A licensed dealer present"],
     "Schedule 3 item 5B covers a person aged 12 to 17 receiving instruction from a category A or B licence holder at an approved range with written consent of a parent or guardian."),
    ("The Firearm Safety Code booklet calls which common belief a myth?",
     "A supervised go is legal anywhere", ["Ammunition must be locked away", "Air rifles count as firearms", "Licences need a safety course"],
     "The booklet says many people believe it is okay to have a go under a licensed person's supervision in any circumstances, but Schedule 3 only allows it at an approved shooting range."),
    ("Under s 126, a person carrying a category A or B longarm must:",
     "Take reasonable steps against theft", ["Keep it in a hard case at all times", "Carry a written carry permit", "Fit a trigger lock in public"],
     "Section 126(1) requires the firearm to be carried and used securely and not dangerously, and reasonable precautions to ensure it is not lost or stolen."),
    ("Which offence does s 132(2) create?",
     "Carrying a hidden firearm for a crime", ["Carrying an uncased firearm", "Carrying a firearm after dark", "Carrying a firearm on a train"],
     "Section 132(2) makes it an offence to carry a firearm concealed from view for the purpose of committing an indictable offence."),
    ("You shoot a letterbox on a country road for fun. Apart from other charges, s 128 makes it an offence to:",
     "Damage property with a firearm", ["Fire within 50 m of a road", "Shoot without a Game Licence", "Use a rifle bigger than .22"],
     "Section 128 says a person must not injure or damage property with a firearm. Using a firearm in a dangerous manner is a separate offence under s 129."),
    ("A person with an unlicensed inherited shotgun leaves it in a hallway cupboard. Section 129A makes it an offence to:",
     "Store it in an insecure manner", ["Keep it longer than 7 days", "Show it to a visitor", "Clean it in the house"],
     "Section 129A makes it an offence for a person who possesses a firearm without a licence authorising that possession to store it or its ammunition in an insecure manner."),
    ("To hunt duck, quail or deer in Victoria, a firearm licence holder also needs:",
     "A Game Licence", ["A category C licence", "A club membership", "A permit to acquire"],
     "The course slides and the booklet say a Game Licence, issued by the Game Management Authority and endorsed for the game types, is needed to hunt duck, quail and deer."),
    ("The course slides say that when camping, backpacking or hiking with firearms you must either take them with you or:",
     "Leave a licensed person in camp", ["Hide them under the tent", "Lock them in the car boot", "Remove one small part only"],
     "The slides say you must leave a licensed person in camp to look after the firearms or take them with you at all times, and take reasonable precautions against loss or theft."),
    ("Changing the details printed on your firearm licence yourself is:",
     "An offence under s 137", ["Allowed for address changes", "Allowed with a witness", "Allowed if you tell a dealer"],
     "Section 137 makes it an offence for anyone other than the Chief Commissioner or a person acting for the Chief Commissioner to alter the particulars on a licence or permit."),
    ("A Tasmanian target shooter brings a licensed rifle to Victoria for a match run by an approved club. Under s 185, they are:",
     "Deemed to hold a licence", ["Unable to take part", "Needing a 28-day permit", "Required to hire a rifle"],
     "Section 185(1) deems an interstate resident with a category A or B licence for sport or target shooting to hold a corresponding Victorian licence to compete in a match run by an approved club."),
    ("An interstate hunting licence holder visiting Victoria may hunt on private land under s 185(2) if they have:",
     "Permission from the owner", ["A Victorian club sponsor", "A dealer's letter of support", "A Victorian home address"],
     "Section 185(2) deems the interstate hunter licensed to hunt on land where they have the permission of the owner or occupier, and on Crown land where hunting is allowed."),
    ("Under s 126(4), anyone carrying cartridge ammunition must make sure it is carried:",
     "Securely and not dangerously", ["In its original packet", "In a locked metal tin", "Well apart from any firearm"],
     "Section 126(4) requires ammunition being carried or used to be handled in a secure, not dangerous way, with reasonable precautions so that it is not lost or stolen."),
]
